The three lower existing reviews do not have a review ID, so the update API cannot be applied to them. I will inspect the full set of existing reviews for those four target songs to identify the correct records and their mutation possibilities.

```python
target_review_ids = {
    review['song_review_id']
    for song_id in target_song_ids
    for review in target_review_records[song_id]
}
target_reviews_by_id = {
    review['song_review_id']: review
    for song_id in target_song_ids
    for review in target_review_records[song_id]
}
rating_summary_existing = {
    'one_star': sum(1 for review in target_reviews_by_id.values() if review['rating'] == 1.0),
    'two_star': sum(1 for review in target_reviews_by_id.values() if review['rating'] == 2.0),
    'three_star': sum(1 for review in target_reviews_by_id.values() if review['rating'] == 3.0),
    'four_star': sum(1 for review in target_reviews_by_id.values() if review['rating'] == 4.0)
}
print({
    'target_review_ids': target_review_ids,
    'rating_summary_existing': rating_summary_existing,
    'reviews_by_id': target_reviews_by_id
})
```
